Pursuant to Section 16, in relation to Sections 477(3)(ix) and 458(3)(ix) of RA No. 7160, as amended, and in the exercise of their mandates to ensure the preservation and enrichment of culture, promote health and safety, and enhance the right of the people to a balanced ecology, the local Sanggunians are hereby enjoined to enact ordinances that supplement national billboard regulations on the following areas:
a. non-obstruction of natural landscape and prohibition of signs or billboards that debase or offend aesthetic and cultural values and traditions;
b. restricted areas or those that distract or obstruct the view of the public as to constitute a traffic hazard, especially along major thoroughfares and public roads;
c. billboard-free zones such as historical sites, tourist destinations and parks, institutional establishments, and critical facilities, such as power plants.
